              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for poverty, then the Marathi for literacy."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: महसूल",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "महसूल — mahsūl — \"revenue; land tax\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सरकारला करातून मोठा महसूल मिळतो. sarkārlā karātūn moṭhā mahsūl miḷto. The government gets a large revenue from taxes."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine: मोठा महसूल (mahsūl); mostly money the state takes in, from taxes and land."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "महसूल (mahsūl) is a loan from Persian, usually traced to Arabic maḥṣūl, \"produce, yield\": what the land yields to the state."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
